---
// Privacy — migrated to the mockup design system (MockupLayout).
import MockupLayout from "../layouts/MockupLayout.astro";

const updated = "October 2026";
---

<MockupLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Ali Samadi Agency"
  description="How Ali Samadi Agency collects, uses, and protects the personal information you share through our website, contact forms, and checkout."
  canonical="https://alisamadii.com/privacy"
  og={{
    title: "Privacy Policy — Ali Samadi Agency",
    description:
      "How Ali Samadi Agency collects, uses, and protects your personal information.",
    url: "https://alisamadii.com/privacy",
    twitterDescription:
      "How Ali Samadi Agency collects, uses, and protects your personal information.",
  }}
>
  <main id="top">
    <!-- Hero -->
    <section style="padding: 140px 0 32px;">
      <div class="wrap" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;text-align:center;gap:18px;">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span></span>Legal</p>
        <h1 class="hero-h1" style="margin:0;max-width:18ch;font-size:clamp(40px,6vw,76px);line-height:1.02;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.035em;">
          Privacy <span style="color:rgb(194,69,31);font-style:italic;">Policy</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="mono" style="margin:0;font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:0.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:rgb(107,102,93);">
          Last updated: {updated}
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Body -->
    <section style="padding: 24px 0 96px; border-top: 1px solid rgba(27,26,23,0.06);">
      <div class="wrap" style="max-width:820px;">
        <div class="prose" style="padding-top:48px;">
          <p>
            Ali Samadi Agency ("we", "us", "our") operates
            <strong>alisamadii.com</strong>. This policy explains what
            personal information we collect, why we collect it, and how you can
            control it. We keep data collection to the minimum needed to respond
            to you and deliver our services.
          </p>

          <h2>Information we collect</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Contact details</strong> you submit through our contact or
              onboarding forms — such as your name, email address, and message.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Billing information</strong> when you start a project. Payments
              are processed by Stripe; we never see or store your full card details.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Basic usage data</strong> (e.g. pages visited) collected by
              privacy-respecting analytics to help us improve the site.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <h2>How we use your information</h2>
          <p>
            We use your information to reply to enquiries, prepare quotes,
            deliver and support projects, process payments, and meet our legal
            and accounting obligations. We do not sell your personal
            information, and we do not use it for advertising.
          </p>

          <h2>Third-party services</h2>
          <p>
            We rely on a small number of trusted providers to run our business
            — including <strong>Stripe</strong> for payments,
            <strong>Google</strong> for optional calendar integration (see
            below), and our hosting and email providers for delivering the site
            and communicating with you. Each processes data only as needed to
            provide their service.
          </p>

          <h2>Google user data (Google Calendar)</h2>
          <p>
            Our client dashboard offers an optional appointment booking feature.
            If you choose to connect your Google account, we request access to
            the following Google Calendar scopes:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Free/busy availability</strong>
              (<code>calendar.freebusy</code>) — read when your calendar is busy
              so the booking widget only offers time slots when you are
              available. We never read event titles, descriptions, attendees, or
              any other event content through this scope.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Calendar events</strong>
              (<code>calendar.events</code>) — create an event on your calendar
              when a visitor confirms a booking, so the appointment appears in
              your schedule with the visitor's name and contact details.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            We use this access solely to power the booking feature you enabled.
            Specifically:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              We store the OAuth tokens Google issues to us, encrypted, in our
              database so the connection keeps working between sessions.
            </li>
            <li>
              We store the bookings created through the widget (date, time,
              visitor name and contact details) in our database so you can see
              them in your dashboard.
            </li>
            <li>
              We do <strong>not</strong> store your calendar contents.
              Availability is checked live at the moment a visitor views the
              booking widget and is not retained.
            </li>
            <li>
              We do not use Google user data for advertising, do not sell it,
              and do not share it with third parties. No humans read this data
              except as needed for security, to comply with the law, or with
              your explicit consent for support.
            </li>
            <li>
              We do not use Google user data to develop, improve, or train
              machine-learning or artificial-intelligence models.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            You can disconnect Google Calendar at any time from your dashboard,
            or revoke our access from your
            <a
              href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer">Google account permissions</a
            >. On disconnection we delete the stored tokens. You can also email
            us to request deletion of any stored booking data.
          </p>
          <p>
            Our use and transfer of information received from Google APIs
            adheres to the
            <a
              href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >Google API Services User Data Policy</a
            >, including the Limited Use requirements.
          </p>

          <h2>Your rights</h2>
          <p>
            You can ask us to access, correct, or delete the personal
            information we hold about you at any time. To make a request, email
            <a href="mailto:agency@alisamadii.com">agency@alisamadii.com</a> and
            we'll respond promptly.
          </p>

          <h2>Contact</h2>
          <p>
            Questions about this policy? Reach us at
            <a href="mailto:agency@alisamadii.com">agency@alisamadii.com</a>, Ali
            Samadi Agency, USA.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</MockupLayout>
